// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root-cause analysis across attempts 1 (40.8%) and 73–75 (2–10%):
//
// Attempt 1 used `next == "<<"` (exact token equality). Tokenizers nearly always
// produce " <<" (space-prefixed) or split "<<" across tokens, so this check
// almost never fires. Generation was effectively UNCONSTRAINED throughout:
// the model's native math reasoning wrote complete formulas like <<n*rate+base>>.
// When the check DID fire, the span closed after 1 token (single identifiers are
// complete expressions in the grammar), but that affected very few spans. 40.8%.
//
// Attempts 73–75 used RenderedEndsWith which fires on EVERY "<<" token. This
// forces constrained mode 15+ times per example. The parser's IsCompletePrefix
// fires after 1 token (e.g., ["n"] is a complete expression), closing each span
// immediately. Result: avg 1.09 tokens/span; the last span is just a variable
// name; the extracted answer is wrong. 2–10%.
//
// Fix: Use FULLY UNCONSTRAINED generation. No RenderedEndsWith, no constrained
// mode, no parser interference. Rely on Qwen2.5-14B's native capability for
// math word problems, guided to write ONE complete formula in ONE << >> span at
// the end. This matches the effective behavior of attempt 1 but with guidance
// explicitly preventing split-span errors (operators between separate << >> spans).
//
// Guidance key points:
//   (1) ONE combined formula in ONE final << >> span
//   (2) WRONG example: <<n1>> * <<rate>> + <<n2>>
//   (3) RIGHT example: <<n1 * rate + n2>>
//   (4) Evaluator extracts only the LAST << >> span
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut := false at init and never changes in the loop.
//   The implication insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//   is vacuously true since the antecedent is always false. No constrained-mode
//   helper is called, so insideConstrainedOut and currentConstrainedOut are never
//   modified. Invariant holds on every branch (there is effectively only one branch:
//   outside-span unconstrained step). ✓
//
// Invariant 2 — progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//   Initialization: |generated| = |generatedPrefix|, steps = 0. 0 <= 0. ✓
//   EOS branch: steps += 1, generated unchanged.
//     |generated| = |generatedPrefix| + (steps - 1) <= |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//   Non-EOS branch: steps += 1, generated grows by exactly 1 token.
//     |generated|_new = |generated|_old + 1 <= |generatedPrefix| + steps_old + 1
//                     = |generatedPrefix| + steps_new. ✓
//   Each UnconstrainedStep consumes exactly 1 token-step (including EOS),
//   so visible growth is at most the consumed token budget. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := false;
currentConstrainedOut := [];
cost := 0;

helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm,
  "Solve this problem step by step. At the very end, write the complete final symbolic answer as a SINGLE combined formula inside << >> delimiters. Put the ENTIRE expression in ONE << >> span. " +
  "WRONG format: <<n1>> * <<rate>> + <<n2>>  (operators between spans). " +
  "RIGHT format: <<n1 * rate + n2>>  (full formula in one span). " +
  "The evaluator reads ONLY the last << >> as your answer, so it must contain the complete combined expression, not just one variable.");

var steps: nat := 0;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut
  invariant currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  var next := helpers.UnconstrainedStep(lm, prompt, generated);
  steps := steps + 1;
  if next == eosToken {
    break;
  }
  generated := generated + [next];
}

cost := steps;

